{"family": "vitmatte", "task": "matting", "name": "ViTMatte", "plain": "ViTMatte (Huazhong University of Science and Technology, 2023): refines a rough trimap (sure background, sure foreground, unknown band) into a soft alpha matte, e.g. hair and fur edges; a plain Vision Transformer plus a small detail decoder; small and base versions. Apache-2.0 code and weights.", "summary": "ViTMatte (Yao et al., HUST, Information Fusion 2024): trimap-based natural image matting. A plain ViT (ViTDet: windowed attention with relative positions plus four global blocks with convolutional residual blocks) sees the image and its trimap as one 4-channel input; a light convolutional detail-capture decoder fuses the ViT features with a full-resolution conv stream into the alpha. Needs a trimap (0 background, 128 unknown, 255 foreground).", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/hustvl/ViTMatte", "upstream_commit": "8cd7ef068380977c3962c4cb733cb1fe7f2241a5", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "ViTMatte: Boosting Image Matting with Pretrained Plain Vision Transformers", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15272", "date": "2023-05-24", "venue": "Information Fusion 2024", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["dpt_fused", "cudnn_hacc", "igev", "cutlass_conv"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [], "outputs": [{"name": "alpha", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": [], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image (trimap-guided models also a trimap: background / unknown / foreground). Output: an alpha matte `[H, W]` in [0, 1] at the input size: 1 = foreground (background removal, dichotomous / salient object segmentation).", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "vitmatte-s", "released": null, "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "vitma